  "_claudeCodeFloorNote": "M34.D: the oldest Claude Code this release supports. Its settings carry \"onFailure\": \"block\" on the red gate, which Claude Code reads from 2.1.295; an older CLI may reject the whole settings file, and a rejected file drops every hook and deny rule. kit-update --ready's cli row reads this value from here (or sbak/release-manifest.json in a project) and never a copy of it.",
  "_fileClassNote": "C.3.5 (ruling 3-strict): every entry declares fileClass payload|repo-identity, FAIL-CLOSED — an unclassified entry is a build error, never a default. payload = the kit machinery; it is what the ZIP carries and what kit-update --adopt installs from. repo-identity = the public repo's own paperwork (README/LICENSE/SECURITY/…/.github); declared here (the public repo and --adopt's route table read it) but NEVER packed. The kit's MIT text ships renamed LICENSE-SBAK.txt so the payload carries its license without colliding with a host repo's LICENSE. This manifest ships in the payload — it IS --adopt's route table in the adopted repo (one source of truth for install and pack).",
